    basic: 'Start with strong hole cards that have flexibility. Three cards of different ranks give you more chances to pair up. Avoid playing hands where all three cards are the same suit (unless very high), as you only have one card to complete a flush.',
    intermediate: "Track potential wild cards. If your hole cards include a 2, 3, or 4, you have a good chance that your cards might become wild. Conversely, holding high cards (T, J, Q, K, A) means you're hoping the community cards stay low.",
    advanced: "The 'Lame Brain' Calculation: When the third community card is revealed, calculate the probability of the fourth card making your hole cards wild. If you hold a 5 and the community shows 8-7-3, there's a good chance your 5 becomes wild if the last card is 2, 3, 4, or 5. Use this to determine whether to bet aggressively or fold.",
